<p><strong>What happens at a hearing</strong></p>
<p>A hearing is an informal discussion led by an Inspector or appointed person.</p>
<p>At a hearing:</p>
<ul>
	<li>anyone can speak and share their views on the application</li>
	<li>the Inspector or appointed person will ask questions to clarify facts and evidence</li>
</ul>
<p>You cannot question or cross-examine other people directly. The Inspector manages the discussion and asks all the questions.</p>
